summary:
- topic: FY2027 Budget Proposal
  text: The administration presented an FY2027 budget proposal designed to meet the
    City Council's guidance of a 6% tax increase. This requires approximately $8.4
    million in reductions from the roll-forward budget, resulting in a proposed 3.3%
    increase over the FY26 budget, the smallest in five years due to the depletion
    of the fund balance.
- topic: Proposed Staff Reductions
  text: To meet the budget targets, the proposal includes a significant reduction
    of 77 positions across the district. This includes 42 teachers, 16 educational
    technicians, 14 service employees (custodial/transportation), and two administrators.
- topic: Elementary School Closure and Reconfiguration
  text: A central component of the budget reduction plan is the closure of one elementary
    school. After community feedback on a previous model, the administration presented
    a revised proposal to close Dyer Elementary School, keeping the remaining four
    schools in a Pre-K/K-4 configuration.
- topic: Fund Balance and Financial Policy
  text: The Assistant Superintendent highlighted that the district's fund balance
    (savings) is depleted after being used to offset tax increases in previous years.
    The leadership team recommended the board adopt new policies to establish minimum
    fund balance thresholds to ensure future financial sustainability.
- topic: Board and Public Concerns
  text: Board members and numerous public commenters expressed significant concerns
    about the magnitude of the cuts, the fast-paced timeline for such a major decision,
    and the potential negative impacts on students and staff. Many advocated for delaying
    a school closure decision until a new superintendent is in place.
- topic: Superintendent Search Update
  text: The Board Chair confirmed that the search for a new superintendent is proceeding.
    The process, guided by Zeal Education Group, will involve confidential interviews
    conducted solely by the school board and its student representatives.
- topic: Community Debate on School Closure
  text: Public comment featured extensive debate over which school, if any, should
    be closed. Arguments for closing Kaler Elementary centered on potential health
    risks from nearby petroleum tanks, while arguments against it focused on the high
    needs of its student population. The proposal to close Dyer Elementary was also
    met with opposition.
- topic: Employee Recognition
  text: The meeting began with a detailed and heartfelt recognition of retiring crossing
    guard Thomas Schmeling for his years of dedicated service ensuring student safety
    at the Frost and Main Street crossing.
